1
00:00:01,466 --> 00:00:03,092
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:03,927 --> 00:00:05,386
Earth...

3
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,305
Fire...

4
00:00:07,847 --> 00:00:09,349
Air.

5
00:00:10,225 --> 00:00:13,770
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:14,354 --> 00:00:18,483
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:18,775 --> 00:00:21,361
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:21,444 --> 00:00:22,695
could stop them.

9
00:00:22,779 --> 00:00:24,531
But when the world
needed him most,

10
00:00:24,614 --> 00:00:25,782
he vanished.

11
00:00:26,199 --> 00:00:27,450
100 years passed,

12
00:00:27,534 --> 00:00:29,994
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar―

13
00:00:30,078 --> 00:00:31,746
An airbender named Aang.

14
00:00:31,829 --> 00:00:33,957
And although his airbending
skills are great,

15
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:36,626
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

16
00:00:36,709 --> 00:00:37,794
AANG: Oof.

17
00:00:37,961 --> 00:00:41,005
But I believe Aang can save the world.

18
00:00:49,597 --> 00:00:51,224
AZULA: If I want to catch my prey,

19
00:00:51,307 --> 00:00:52,976
I must be agile, nimble.

20
00:00:53,059 --> 00:00:55,019
I need a small elite team.

21
00:00:56,938 --> 00:01:00,567
TOPH: Even though I was born blind,
I've never had a problem seeing.

22
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:02,569
I see with earthbending.

23
00:01:03,236 --> 00:01:05,446
AANG: You're going to be
a great teacher, Toph.

24
00:01:05,863 --> 00:01:07,782
I thought a lot about
what you said.

25
00:01:07,865 --> 00:01:09,784
You did? Good, good.

26
00:01:10,034 --> 00:01:12,704
We no longer have
anything to gain by traveling together.

27
00:01:13,788 --> 00:01:15,415
I need to find my own way.

28
00:01:29,596 --> 00:01:32,015
Hey, you guys picked
a great campsite.

29
00:01:32,473 --> 00:01:34,267
The grass is so soft.

30
00:01:34,475 --> 00:01:36,853
That's not grass. Appa's shedding.

31
00:01:36,936 --> 00:01:38,146
Oh, gross.

32
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:39,606
AANG: That's not gross.

33
00:01:39,689 --> 00:01:41,482
It's just a part of spring.

34
00:01:41,566 --> 00:01:43,234
You know, rebirth,
flowers blooming,

35
00:01:43,318 --> 00:01:44,861
and Appa gets a new coat.

36
00:01:45,153 --> 00:01:47,488
Ahh. The beauty of spring.

37
00:01:48,781 --> 00:01:50,241
( GROWLING )

38
00:01:51,534 --> 00:01:52,952
Stop. Appa, stop!

39
00:01:53,036 --> 00:01:55,121
( COUGHING )

40
00:01:55,204 --> 00:01:58,750
It's not that bad, Katara.
It makes a great wig.

41
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:00,251
And a great beard.

42
00:02:00,335 --> 00:02:01,711
( BOYS LAUGHING )

43
00:02:01,794 --> 00:02:04,714
I'm just glad we finally have
another girl in the group,

44
00:02:04,797 --> 00:02:06,466
because you two are disgusting.

45
00:02:07,467 --> 00:02:09,594
Excuse me.
Does anyone have a razor,

46
00:02:09,677 --> 00:02:12,680
because I got some hairy pits.

47
00:02:12,764 --> 00:02:14,307
( LAUGHTER )

48
00:02:14,390 --> 00:02:15,558
( SNEEZES )

49
00:02:18,394 --> 00:02:19,812
( CHUCKLES )

50
00:02:30,198 --> 00:02:32,533
So, Toph, usually when
setting up camp,

51
00:02:32,617 --> 00:02:34,160
we try to divide up the work.

52
00:02:34,744 --> 00:02:37,872
Hey, don't worry about me. I'm good to go.

53
00:02:37,955 --> 00:02:40,208
Well, actually, what I'm trying to say is

54
00:02:40,291 --> 00:02:42,043
some of us might fetch water

55
00:02:42,126 --> 00:02:44,212
while someone else
might set up the fire pit

56
00:02:44,295 --> 00:02:45,296
or put up the tent.

57
00:02:45,630 --> 00:02:47,340
Even Momo does his fair share.

58
00:02:47,715 --> 00:02:50,635
Katara, I'm fine.
I can carry my own weight.

59
00:02:50,718 --> 00:02:53,429
I don't need a fire.
I've already collected my own food.

60
00:02:53,638 --> 00:02:57,100
And look. My tent's all set up.

61
00:02:57,183 --> 00:03:00,103
Well, that's great for you,
but we still need to finish―

62
00:03:00,186 --> 00:03:02,897
I don't understand.
What's the problem here?

63
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:04,357
Never mind.

64
00:03:09,362 --> 00:03:10,738
Oops. Sorry.

65
00:03:16,869 --> 00:03:19,664
Hey, Toph, I wanted to apologize
for earlier.

66
00:03:19,747 --> 00:03:21,582
I think we're all just a little tired

67
00:03:21,666 --> 00:03:23,292
and getting on each
other's nerves.

68
00:03:23,376 --> 00:03:25,753
Yeah. You do seem pretty tired.

69
00:03:26,504 --> 00:03:27,880
I meant all of us.

70
00:03:28,089 --> 00:03:30,341
Well, good night.

71
00:03:31,175 --> 00:03:32,468
Good night.

72
00:03:43,062 --> 00:03:44,897
There's something coming toward us.

73
00:03:45,189 --> 00:03:46,482
AANG: What is it?

74
00:03:46,566 --> 00:03:51,070
It feels like an avalanche,
but also not an avalanche.

75
00:03:51,571 --> 00:03:54,031
Your powers of perception
are frightening.

76
00:03:54,490 --> 00:03:55,700
Should we leave?

77
00:03:55,783 --> 00:03:57,034
Better safe than sorry.

78
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:03,916
What is that thing?

79
00:04:08,171 --> 00:04:09,213
( SNORING )

80
00:04:10,006 --> 00:04:11,132
( YAWNS )

81
00:04:19,974 --> 00:04:22,810
Ah, land, sweet land.

82
00:04:23,686 --> 00:04:25,104
See you guys in the morning.

83
00:04:25,188 --> 00:04:26,856
Actually, can you help us unload?

84
00:04:26,939 --> 00:04:29,400
Really? You need me to help unload

85
00:04:29,484 --> 00:04:31,527
Sokka's funky-smelling sleeping bag?

86
00:04:32,028 --> 00:04:33,029
( SNIFFS )

87
00:04:33,112 --> 00:04:34,363
Well, yeah.

88
00:04:35,198 --> 00:04:36,449
That and everything else.

89
00:04:36,532 --> 00:04:38,201
You're a part of our team now and―

90
00:04:38,284 --> 00:04:40,995
Look, I didn't ask you to unload my stuff.

91
00:04:41,078 --> 00:04:42,580
I'm carrying
my own weight.

92
00:04:42,663 --> 00:04:43,998
That's not the point.

93
00:04:44,457 --> 00:04:45,708
Ever since you joined us,

94
00:04:45,792 --> 00:04:48,211
you've been nothing
but selfish and unhelpful.

95
00:04:48,294 --> 00:04:51,088
What? Look here, sugar queen.

96
00:04:51,172 --> 00:04:52,965
I gave up everything I had

97
00:04:53,049 --> 00:04:55,009
so that I could teach Aang earthbending.

98
00:04:55,092 --> 00:04:58,387
So don't you talk to me
about being selfish.

99
00:04:59,972 --> 00:05:01,265
"Sugar queen"?!

100
00:05:02,141 --> 00:05:05,019
D―did you just slam the door in my face?

101
00:05:05,353 --> 00:05:07,939
How can you be so infuriating?

102
00:05:08,356 --> 00:05:10,483
Should we do something?

103
00:05:10,566 --> 00:05:12,193
Hey, I'm just enjoying the show.

104
00:05:12,985 --> 00:05:15,905
Ok, ok. You both need to calm down.

105
00:05:16,155 --> 00:05:18,157
Both?! I'm completely calm!

106
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:21,035
I can see that.

107
00:05:26,791 --> 00:05:29,377
The stars sure are
beautiful tonight.

108
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,504
Too bad you can't see them, Toph.

109
00:05:31,587 --> 00:05:32,672
( TOPH GRUNTS )

110
00:05:32,755 --> 00:05:33,881
( KATARA SCREAMS )

111
00:05:34,549 --> 00:05:36,300
Hey, how's a guy supposed to sleep

112
00:05:36,384 --> 00:05:38,594
with all this yelling and earthquaking?

113
00:05:39,804 --> 00:05:40,972
That thing is back.

114
00:05:41,472 --> 00:05:43,182
Well, how far away is it?

115
00:05:43,266 --> 00:05:46,644
Maybe we can close our eyes
just for a few minutes.

116
00:05:47,645 --> 00:05:49,397
AANG: I don't think so, Sokka.

117
00:05:55,278 --> 00:05:57,363
Seriously, what is that thing?

118
00:05:57,446 --> 00:05:59,574
And how does it keep finding us?

119
00:06:00,032 --> 00:06:02,201
I don't know, but this time,

120
00:06:02,285 --> 00:06:04,120
I'm gonna make sure we lose them.

121
00:06:19,510 --> 00:06:21,762
SOKKA: Ok, forget about setting up camp.

122
00:06:21,846 --> 00:06:25,308
I'm finding the softest pile of dirt
and going to sleep.

123
00:06:25,808 --> 00:06:28,394
That's good, because Toph wasn't
going to help anyway.

124
00:06:28,477 --> 00:06:32,273
Oh, I didn't realize baby still needed
someone to tuck her in bed.

125
00:06:32,356 --> 00:06:34,358
Come on, guys. There's something after us,

126
00:06:34,442 --> 00:06:36,777
and we don't even
know what or who it is.

127
00:06:37,153 --> 00:06:40,239
It could be Zuko.
We haven't seen him since the north pole.

128
00:06:40,323 --> 00:06:41,574
Who's Zuko?

129
00:06:41,657 --> 00:06:43,743
Oh, just some angry freak
with a ponytail

130
00:06:43,826 --> 00:06:45,703
who's tracked us all over the world.

131
00:06:45,786 --> 00:06:48,623
What's wrong with ponytails, ponytail?

132
00:06:48,706 --> 00:06:51,876
This is a warrior's wolf tail.

133
00:06:51,959 --> 00:06:54,295
Well, it certainly tells
the other warriors

134
00:06:54,378 --> 00:06:56,130
that you're fun and perky.

135
00:06:56,547 --> 00:06:59,675
Anyway, whoever's chasing us,
they couldn't have followed us here,

136
00:06:59,759 --> 00:07:03,012
so, now, would everyone just shush?

137
00:07:03,846 --> 00:07:05,473
( MOMO CHATTERING )

138
00:07:05,556 --> 00:07:09,852
No, Momo. Shh. Sleepy time.

139
00:07:14,482 --> 00:07:16,192
Oh, don't tell me.

140
00:07:16,275 --> 00:07:19,487
That's impossible.
There's no way they could have tracked us.

141
00:07:19,570 --> 00:07:22,073
I can feel it with my own two feet.

142
00:07:28,746 --> 00:07:29,914
Let's get out of here.

143
00:07:29,997 --> 00:07:32,458
Maybe we should face them
and find out who they are.

144
00:07:32,541 --> 00:07:34,168
Who knows? Maybe they're friendly.

145
00:07:34,251 --> 00:07:35,753
Always the optimist.

146
00:07:56,649 --> 00:07:58,484
( LIZARDS HISSING )

147
00:08:01,362 --> 00:08:03,197
It's those three girls from Omashu.

148
00:08:03,739 --> 00:08:06,492
We can take them― Three on three.

149
00:08:06,575 --> 00:08:08,327
Actually, Toph, there's four of us.

150
00:08:08,411 --> 00:08:10,663
Oh, I'm sorry. I didn't count you.

151
00:08:10,746 --> 00:08:12,164
You know, no bending and all.

152
00:08:12,248 --> 00:08:13,916
I can still fight!

153
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,460
Ok, three on three plus Sokka.

154
00:08:16,544 --> 00:08:17,545
( SOKKA GROWLS )

155
00:08:22,925 --> 00:08:25,761
Well, we wanted to find out who they were,
and we found out.

156
00:08:25,845 --> 00:08:27,138
Now, let's get out of here.

157
00:08:40,401 --> 00:08:41,527
Appa, yip yip!

158
00:08:50,286 --> 00:08:54,081
KATARA: I can't believe those girls
followed us all the way from Omashu.

159
00:08:54,165 --> 00:08:56,667
I still think we
could have taken them.

160
00:08:56,751 --> 00:08:59,378
Are you kidding me?
The crazy blue firebending

161
00:08:59,462 --> 00:09:01,756
and the flying daggers
are bad enough,

162
00:09:01,839 --> 00:09:03,340
but the last time we saw them,

163
00:09:03,632 --> 00:09:06,427
one of those girls
did something that took my bending away.

164
00:09:06,510 --> 00:09:07,511
That's scary.

165
00:09:07,803 --> 00:09:10,347
SOKKA: Oh, no. The sun is rising.

166
00:09:10,431 --> 00:09:12,641
We've been up all night
with no sleep.

167
00:09:13,267 --> 00:09:14,560
Sokka, we'll be ok.

168
00:09:15,019 --> 00:09:16,062
Are you sure?

169
00:09:16,145 --> 00:09:17,646
I've never not slept before.

170
00:09:17,730 --> 00:09:19,982
What if I fall asleep now
and something happens?

171
00:09:20,066 --> 00:09:22,109
And something always happens!

172
00:09:22,359 --> 00:09:24,570
Every time we land,
those girls are there.

173
00:09:24,653 --> 00:09:26,447
So we'll just have
to keep flying.

174
00:09:27,114 --> 00:09:28,908
AANG: We can't keep flying forever.

175
00:09:35,247 --> 00:09:37,208
( CALLING )

176
00:09:43,839 --> 00:09:45,007
( AANG YAWNS )

177
00:09:45,758 --> 00:09:47,176
So what's our plan?

178
00:09:47,259 --> 00:09:48,761
Don't know.

179
00:09:48,844 --> 00:09:50,596
Too tired to think.

180
00:09:50,805 --> 00:09:53,724
I'm sure we'll come up with something
after a short nap.

181
00:09:54,558 --> 00:09:56,769
Yes! Sleep.

182
00:10:01,190 --> 00:10:02,942
What's going on?!

183
00:10:03,025 --> 00:10:04,652
Appa fell asleep.

184
00:10:04,735 --> 00:10:06,070
( KIDS SCREAMING )

185
00:10:09,031 --> 00:10:10,032
Wake up, buddy!

186
00:10:10,449 --> 00:10:12,159
( KIDS SCREAMING )

187
00:10:27,174 --> 00:10:28,968
Appa's exhausted.

188
00:10:29,385 --> 00:10:32,638
Ok, we've put a lot of distance
between us and them.

189
00:10:33,097 --> 00:10:36,642
The plan right now is to follow
Appa's lead and get some sleep.

190
00:10:36,725 --> 00:10:39,103
Of course, we could have
gotten some sleep earlier

191
00:10:39,186 --> 00:10:40,938
if Toph didn't have such issues.

192
00:10:41,355 --> 00:10:42,356
What?!

193
00:10:42,690 --> 00:10:45,401
All right, all right!
Everyone's exhausted.

194
00:10:45,484 --> 00:10:47,194
Let's just get some rest.

195
00:10:47,403 --> 00:10:50,239
No. I want to hear what Katara has to say.

196
00:10:50,698 --> 00:10:52,241
You think I have issues?

197
00:10:52,616 --> 00:10:55,077
I'm just saying,
maybe if you helped out earlier,

198
00:10:55,161 --> 00:10:57,955
we could have set up our camp faster
and gotten some sleep.

199
00:10:58,038 --> 00:11:00,374
And then maybe we wouldn't
be in this situation.

200
00:11:00,791 --> 00:11:02,418
TOPH: You're blaming me for this?

201
00:11:04,962 --> 00:11:07,464
No. No! She's not blaming you.

202
00:11:07,548 --> 00:11:08,632
No, I'm blaming her.

203
00:11:08,716 --> 00:11:09,842
- Hey!
- Uh!

204
00:11:09,925 --> 00:11:11,760
I never asked you for diddly-dooda.

205
00:11:11,844 --> 00:11:13,262
I carry my own weight.

206
00:11:13,804 --> 00:11:17,349
Besides, if there's anyone to blame,
it's Sheddy over here.

207
00:11:17,433 --> 00:11:19,351
AANG: What? You're blaming Appa?

208
00:11:19,727 --> 00:11:22,146
Yeah. You want to know
how they keep finding us?

209
00:11:22,229 --> 00:11:24,648
He's leaving a trail
everywhere we go.

210
00:11:25,024 --> 00:11:28,402
How dare you blame Appa.
He saved your life three times today.

211
00:11:28,485 --> 00:11:30,696
If there's anyone to blame, it's you.

212
00:11:31,155 --> 00:11:33,908
You're always talking
about how you carry your own weight,

213
00:11:33,991 --> 00:11:36,702
But you're not. He is.
Appa's carrying your weight.

214
00:11:36,994 --> 00:11:40,039
He never had a problem
flying when it was just the three of us.

215
00:11:41,457 --> 00:11:42,958
I'm out of here.

216
00:11:44,919 --> 00:11:45,920
Wait.

217
00:11:59,433 --> 00:12:00,893
What did I just do?

218
00:12:01,143 --> 00:12:03,729
I can't believe
I yelled at my earthbending teacher.

219
00:12:03,812 --> 00:12:05,481
Now she's gone.

220
00:12:05,564 --> 00:12:09,360
I know. We're all
just trying to get used to each other.

221
00:12:09,443 --> 00:12:11,070
And I was so mean to her.

222
00:12:11,737 --> 00:12:14,031
Yeah, you two were pretty much jerks.

223
00:12:14,114 --> 00:12:15,908
- Thanks, Sokka.
- No problem.

224
00:12:16,408 --> 00:12:18,619
We need to find
Toph and apologize.

225
00:12:18,702 --> 00:12:20,621
Ok, but what are we gonna do

226
00:12:20,704 --> 00:12:23,123
about the tank full
of dangerous ladies chasing us?

227
00:12:25,626 --> 00:12:26,835
I have a plan.

228
00:12:37,221 --> 00:12:38,222
Ugh.

229
00:12:38,681 --> 00:12:42,226
AANG: Toph was right. Appa's fur
was leading a trail right to us.

230
00:12:42,685 --> 00:12:44,687
But now that he's clean,
no more trail.

231
00:12:44,770 --> 00:12:46,772
KATARA: Are you sure he's ok to fly?

232
00:12:47,189 --> 00:12:50,401
He'll be fine as long as we leave
his saddle and all our stuff here.

233
00:12:50,484 --> 00:12:54,029
I'm gonna use Appa's fur to make
a fake trail and lead the tank off-course.

234
00:13:14,967 --> 00:13:15,968
Uh!

235
00:13:17,303 --> 00:13:18,512
Ohh.

236
00:13:19,263 --> 00:13:22,224
That really hurt my tailbone.

237
00:13:27,146 --> 00:13:29,023
Wads of wet fur.

238
00:13:29,398 --> 00:13:30,566
How delightful.

239
00:13:30,941 --> 00:13:35,863
Hmm, they're not wads.
They're more like bundles.

240
00:13:35,946 --> 00:13:37,823
Or bunches?

241
00:13:37,906 --> 00:13:39,908
It's got an "uh" sound.

242
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:42,494
Clumps.

243
00:13:42,578 --> 00:13:45,039
Clumps! They're clumps!

244
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,503
The trail goes this way.

245
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:58,719
The Avatar is trying
to give us the slip.

246
00:13:58,802 --> 00:14:01,972
You two head in that direction
and keep your eye out for the bison.

247
00:14:02,598 --> 00:14:04,350
I'll follow this trail.

248
00:15:06,995 --> 00:15:08,705
Toph couldn't have
made it too far.

249
00:15:08,789 --> 00:15:09,873
( SCREECHES )

250
00:15:09,957 --> 00:15:11,542
What is it, Momo?! Oh, no!

251
00:15:12,042 --> 00:15:13,460
Katara!

252
00:15:13,544 --> 00:15:15,254
How did they find us?

253
00:15:16,755 --> 00:15:19,007
SOKKA: Appa, come on.
We need to go faster.

254
00:15:19,091 --> 00:15:20,717
KATARA: He's too tired.

255
00:15:20,801 --> 00:15:22,261
Not good, not good!

256
00:15:24,930 --> 00:15:26,974
We just need to make it
across that river.

257
00:15:28,142 --> 00:15:29,977
Come on, Appa! Just a little further.

258
00:15:35,941 --> 00:15:36,942
Whoa!

259
00:15:43,449 --> 00:15:45,075
SOKKA: We made it. We're safe.

260
00:15:45,159 --> 00:15:46,660
KATARA: You did it, Appa!

261
00:16:28,827 --> 00:16:30,162
Good try, but no.

262
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:39,421
How you doing?

263
00:16:39,505 --> 00:16:40,672
Well, you know.

264
00:16:41,215 --> 00:16:43,675
I thought when Ty Lee and I finally
caught you guys,

265
00:16:43,759 --> 00:16:45,594
it would be more exciting.

266
00:16:45,677 --> 00:16:48,138
Oh, well, victory is boring.

267
00:16:48,889 --> 00:16:50,349
- Aah!
- Aah!

268
00:16:53,393 --> 00:16:55,896
Thanks, Appa.
I don't know what we'd do without you.

269
00:17:01,276 --> 00:17:03,862
Was it just me,
or was that guy kind of cute?

270
00:17:20,170 --> 00:17:21,964
All right. You've caught up with me.

271
00:17:22,047 --> 00:17:23,882
Now, who are you,
and what do you want?

272
00:17:24,550 --> 00:17:28,345
You mean, you haven't guessed?
You don't see the family resemblance.

273
00:17:28,428 --> 00:17:29,805
Here's a hint.

274
00:17:29,888 --> 00:17:31,723
( IMITATING ZUKO )
I must find the Avatar

275
00:17:31,807 --> 00:17:33,183
to restore my honor.

276
00:17:34,309 --> 00:17:36,186
( REGULAR VOICE ) It's ok. You can laugh.

277
00:17:36,353 --> 00:17:37,354
It's funny.

278
00:17:38,146 --> 00:17:39,398
So what now?

279
00:17:39,481 --> 00:17:43,986
Now? Now it's over.
You're tired, and you have no place to go.

280
00:17:44,236 --> 00:17:46,029
You can run, but I'll catch you.

281
00:17:47,281 --> 00:17:48,657
I'm not running.

282
00:17:58,292 --> 00:18:00,127
Here is your tea.

283
00:18:02,254 --> 00:18:05,716
You seem a little
too young to be traveling alone.

284
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,343
You seem a little too old.

285
00:18:09,094 --> 00:18:10,554
Ha ha ha!

286
00:18:10,637 --> 00:18:12,264
Perhaps I am.

287
00:18:13,307 --> 00:18:14,766
I know what you're thinking,

288
00:18:14,850 --> 00:18:17,311
I look like I can't handle
being by myself.

289
00:18:17,894 --> 00:18:19,396
I wasn't thinking that.

290
00:18:19,855 --> 00:18:22,524
You wouldn't let me pour
my own cup of tea.

291
00:18:23,066 --> 00:18:26,570
I poured your tea
because I wanted to

292
00:18:26,653 --> 00:18:28,572
and for no other reason.

293
00:18:29,072 --> 00:18:31,199
People see me
and think I'm weak.

294
00:18:31,283 --> 00:18:32,909
They want to take care of me,

295
00:18:32,993 --> 00:18:36,163
but I can take care of myself by myself.

296
00:18:36,496 --> 00:18:38,332
You sound like my nephew,

297
00:18:38,790 --> 00:18:42,294
Always thinking
you need to do things on your own

298
00:18:42,377 --> 00:18:44,796
without anyone's support.

299
00:18:45,047 --> 00:18:49,635
There is nothing wrong
with letting people who love you help you.

300
00:18:49,968 --> 00:18:52,846
Not that I love you.
Well, I just met you.

301
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:54,431
( CHUCKLES )

302
00:18:54,681 --> 00:18:57,017
So where is your nephew?

303
00:18:57,476 --> 00:18:59,519
I've been tracking him, actually.

304
00:18:59,853 --> 00:19:01,104
Is he lost?

305
00:19:02,105 --> 00:19:03,857
Yes, a little bit.

306
00:19:04,358 --> 00:19:07,110
His life has recently changed,

307
00:19:07,194 --> 00:19:10,280
And he's going through
very difficult times.

308
00:19:10,781 --> 00:19:14,117
He's trying to figure out who he is,

309
00:19:14,201 --> 00:19:15,702
and he went away.

310
00:19:16,036 --> 00:19:17,996
So now you're following him.

311
00:19:18,497 --> 00:19:21,625
I know he doesn't
want me around right now,

312
00:19:21,708 --> 00:19:24,836
but if he needs me, I'll be there.

313
00:19:25,128 --> 00:19:27,381
Your nephew is very lucky,

314
00:19:27,464 --> 00:19:28,757
even if he doesn't know it.

315
00:19:30,509 --> 00:19:31,551
Thank you.

316
00:19:31,635 --> 00:19:35,847
My pleasure. Sharing tea
with a fascinating stranger

317
00:19:35,931 --> 00:19:39,017
is one of life's true delights.

318
00:19:39,101 --> 00:19:41,311
No. Thank you for what you said.

319
00:19:41,978 --> 00:19:44,731
- It helped me.
- I'm glad.

320
00:19:45,649 --> 00:19:48,610
Oh, and about your nephew,

321
00:19:48,694 --> 00:19:51,113
maybe you should tell him
that you need him, too.

322
00:19:55,659 --> 00:19:57,119
( LIZARD HISSING )

323
00:19:59,329 --> 00:20:01,289
Do you really want to fight me?

324
00:20:02,958 --> 00:20:05,627
Yes. I really do.

325
00:20:06,002 --> 00:20:07,003
Zuko!

326
00:20:07,087 --> 00:20:09,131
I was wondering
when you'd show up, Zu-Zu.

327
00:20:09,631 --> 00:20:11,466
Ha ha. Zu-zu?

328
00:20:11,883 --> 00:20:14,511
Back off, Azula. He's mine.

329
00:20:15,721 --> 00:20:17,973
I'm not going anywhere.

330
00:21:06,772 --> 00:21:08,523
( YELLS )

331
00:21:19,993 --> 00:21:21,661
Whoa! Aah!

332
00:21:42,974 --> 00:21:44,601
Aah!

333
00:21:58,782 --> 00:21:59,908
Katara!

334
00:22:10,919 --> 00:22:12,170
Uncle.

335
00:22:12,254 --> 00:22:13,672
Get up.

336
00:22:24,307 --> 00:22:26,351
I thought you guys
could use a little help.

337
00:22:26,726 --> 00:22:27,811
Thanks.

338
00:22:36,778 --> 00:22:38,697
Well, look at this.

339
00:22:38,780 --> 00:22:41,867
Enemies and traitors all working together.

340
00:22:42,742 --> 00:22:45,203
I'm done.
I know when I'm beaten.

341
00:22:45,537 --> 00:22:49,249
You got me.
A princess surrenders with honor.

342
00:22:56,548 --> 00:22:57,716
Aah!

343
00:22:58,675 --> 00:22:59,676
( YELLS )

344
00:23:15,901 --> 00:23:17,193
Get away from us!

345
00:23:22,574 --> 00:23:23,992
Zuko, I can help.

346
00:23:24,743 --> 00:23:26,328
Leave!
